0..77 Comment "// Definitions a Rust caller runs on its own values, and a Rust function they"
78..112 Comment "// call, admitted against its row."
113..115 Comment "//"
116..194 Comment "// The first direction: Rust holds the composed program and calls a definition"
195..273 Comment "// by name. The second: the `extern` block declares the Rust caller\'s `add` as"
274..348 Comment "// an operation of the interface `Boundary`, and `quadrupled` performs it."
349..426 Comment "// Outside a handler the run offers it to the Rust caller\'s host, which calls"
427..498 Comment "// its own `add`. The block names `add`\'s row, and its check admits the"
499..577 Comment "// declared types against the row under Rust\'s default layout. A `u32` crosses"
578..644 Comment "// as itself, and `by-layout.gandr` reads values by their layouts."
645..647 Comment "//"
648..724 Comment "// The Rust test composes this source, names each definition and calls it on"
725..802 Comment "// values it builds, then reads the answer back. Each `runs` item below makes"
803..880 Comment "// the same call from gandr, so both sides state one answer. `quadrupled` has"
881..959 Comment "// none, since only the Rust caller answers `Boundary` there. `mocked` handles"
960..1038 Comment "// `Boundary` in gandr, so its clause answers each `add`, and the run needs no"
1039..1047 Comment "// host."
1048..1050 Comment "//"
1051..1130 Comment "// - see: `model/interop/boundary/by-layout.gandr` — values crossing by their"
1131..1143 Comment "//   layouts"
1144..1219 Comment "// - see: `crates/surface-dispatcher/tests/boundary.rs` — the Rust caller"
1220..1298 Comment "// - see: `library/std/src/boundary.gandr` — `admitBlock`, which the block\'s"
1299..1314 Comment "//   check runs"
1315..1392 Comment "// - see: `model/interop/boundary/function-row.gandr` — the function row an"
1393..1426 Comment "//   `extern` is admitted against"
1428..1502 Comment "// The boundary check reads `admitBlock` here, whatever the listing names."
